---
// The 1.x note on bubbling state events (DECISIONS D25, API audit M9): one per page that
// documents an element's state events. Every listener in the docs scripts carries the guard.
interface Props {
  /** The state events this page's elements fire, e.g. ['open-change']. */
  events: string[];
}

const { events } = Astro.props;
---

<p class="docs-note" role="note">
  {
    events.map((event, i) => (
      <>
        {i > 0 && (i === events.length - 1 ? ' and ' : ', ')}
        <code>{event}</code>
      </>
    ))
  }{' '}{events.length > 1 ? 'bubble' : 'bubbles'} in 1.x, like every state event: a listener on
  an element also hears the same event from an element nested inside it, such as a tooltip in a
  dialog or a time picker in a tab panel. Check the target first:{' '}
  <code>if (e.target !== host) return;</code>. DECISIONS D25 proposes that 2.0 stop bubbling state
  events; item events such as <code>action</code> keep bubbling.
</p>
